# TKTS: `usp_Get_Rental_Inquiries` (client): add to your existing client classes

Input: `p_Session_Key`, `p_Location_Function_Id`. Output: `p_Result_Code`, plus a result set with
`Location_Id, Parent_Location_Id, Position, Rental_Booking_Id, Rental_Inquiry_Id`
(the location and its parent locations, each with its inquiries and bookings).

Endpoint: `POST /api/v1/rental-amenities/inquiries/get`
There are no date columns in the result, so no timezone conversion is needed.

## Spring Boot

### 1. TicketRequest
`sessionKey` and `locationFunctionId` already exist, so there is nothing to add.

### 2. RentalAmenityController
```java
@Operation(summary = "Get Rental Inquiries")
@PostMapping("/inquiries/get")
public ApiResponse<List<Map<String, Object>>> getRentalInquiries(@RequestBody TicketRequest req,
                                                                 @AuthenticationPrincipal Jwt jwt) {
    if (jwt != null) {
        req.setSessionKey(jwt.getClaims().get("origin_jti").toString());
    }
    return ApiResponse.success("Rental Inquiries", rentalAmenityService.getRentalInquiries(req));
}
```

