## Things to check in the stored procedure
These come from my reading of your screenshots, which were angled and partly blurry. Please check the real file.
- The permission check passes `@Location_Function_Id`, but the parameter is `p_Location_Function_Id`. As written, the user variable is NULL, so the check may fail or behave oddly.
- The first query in the recursive CTE uses `WHERE Location_Id = @Location`, but the variable set above is `@Location_Id`.
- The booking join reads `ON RenBoo.Rental_Inquiry = RenInq.Rental_Inquiry`, but the column is probably `Rental_Inquiry_Id`.
- The result has no inquiry details (contact name, event title, dates and so on). It returns only ids. If the UI needs details, ask the DB team to extend the select.




@Override
public List<Map<String, Object>> getRentalInquiries(TicketRequest req) {
    List<Map<String, Object>> rows = rentalAmenityDao.getRentalInquiries(req);
    for (Map<String, Object> row : rows) {
        String tz = (String) row.get("timezone");
        row.put("rentalStartAt", TimezoneConverter.toLocal((LocalDateTime) row.get("rentalStartAt"), tz));
        row.put("rentalEndAt", TimezoneConverter.toLocal((LocalDateTime) row.get("rentalEndAt"), tz));
    }
    return rows;
}

